# datum: the built binary (~150 MB) and any local store.
#
# ⚠ THESE PATTERNS ARE DELIBERATELY BROAD, and that is a scar. The rename moved the
# built binary from `fa/fa` to `datum/fa`, which matched NEITHER the old ignore
# (`fa/fa`) nor the new one (`datum/datum`) — so `git add -A` committed a 144.8 MB
# binary, and GitHub's 100 MB limit is what caught it rather than any check of mine.
# Ignore the binary by SHAPE (an executable in the module dir), not by one exact name.
datum/datum
datum/fa
datum/datum.test
datum/*.test
.datum-db/
.fa-db/
